#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2338 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "Synthetic SNDIGVER codelist terms taken verbatim from SEND CT C89982. Row 1: the SNDIGVER record carries the exact CT submission value -> clean. Row 2: a different parameter (SSPONSOR) whose value is not a SNDIGVER term -> outside the TSPARMCD guard. Row 3: SNDIGVER with an empty TSVAL (null flavour carried elsewhere) -> guarded out by non_empty. Paired with FDA-SE2338-invalid-TS.cdt so a missing codelist cannot make this pass vacuously."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#library codelist-terms SNDIGVER "SEND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE VERSION 3.0" "SEND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE VERSION 3.1" "SEND ANIMAL RULE IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE VERSION 1.0"
dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | SNDIGVER | SEND Implementation Guide Version | SEND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE VERSION 3.1
S1 | TS | 1 | SSPONSOR | Study Sponsor                     | ACME LABS
S1 | TS | 2 | SNDIGVER | SEND Implementation Guide Version |
